# CMOS INVERTER LAYOUT

## Project Title
Design and Layout of CMOS Inverter

## Abstract
This project explains the design and layout of a CMOS inverter using Complementary Metal Oxide Semiconductor (CMOS) technology. A CMOS inverter is a basic digital logic gate used in electronic circuits and VLSI systems. It converts logic HIGH input into logic LOW output and logic LOW input into logic HIGH output. The CMOS inverter is designed using PMOS and NMOS transistors for low power consumption and high efficiency.

## Objective
- To understand the working of CMOS inverter.
- To design CMOS inverter layout.
- To analyze the input-output characteristics of CMOS inverter.
- To study CMOS technology used in digital electronics.

## Components Used
### Hardware
- CMOS Transistors (PMOS and NMOS)
- Power Supply (VDD)
- Ground (GND)

### Software
- Microwind / Cadence / Electric VLSI Tool
- CMOS Layout Design Software

## Working Principle
A CMOS inverter consists of one PMOS transistor connected to VDD and one NMOS transistor connected to Ground (GND).

### Working:
1. When input is LOW (0):
   - PMOS turns ON
   - NMOS turns OFF
   - Output becomes HIGH (1)

2. When input is HIGH (1):
   - PMOS turns OFF
   - NMOS turns ON
   - Output becomes LOW (0)

Thus, the circuit works as an inverter by reversing the input signal.

## CMOS Inverter Circuit
The CMOS inverter consists of:
- PMOS transistor connected to VDD
- NMOS transistor connected to GND
- Input connected to both gates
- Output taken from common drain terminal

